  "labeler_notes": "Titles are 'Hardware Group No. NNN' (10 are 'Hardware Group No.NNN [BULLETIN 023, 251218]' with no space; bulletin tag dropped from the id). No set has a printed description. Struck-out rows excluded (checked on page images and by detecting drawn lines through the text): the 'POWER SUPPLY - AS REQUIRED / BY DIVISION 28 / B/O' row in 001 (p.21), 029 (p.40), 030 (p.40) and 035 (p.43); in 035 also the 'KEYED CONSTRUCTION CORE' row, the 'GASKETING SET 188SBK PSA' row and the 'MEETING STILE 8193AA (2 PCS - 1 SET)' row (p.43). The unstruck bold '[BULLETIN 023, 251218]' tag printed next to those deleted rows is ignored with the row. Bold added rows keep their '[BULLETIN 023, 251218]' tag inside catalog_number because it is printed in that column (e.g. POWER SUPPLY 'PS904 ... 120/240 VAC [BULLETIN 023, 251218]'). Set 034 has NO struck-out rows (the struck rows on p.43 belong to set 035); set 035 (pp.43-44) was added as an extra set so the key has a set with several struck rows. 'NOTE:' pseudo-rows at the end of a list (NOTE: in the DESCRIPTION column, text in CATALOG column, e.g. 'FURNISH 5BB1HW 5\" X 4.5\" HINGES AT DOORS OVER 3'0\" WIDE') are general set-level notes about hinges/seals, not about the row above, so they are excluded (034 pp.42-43, 035 p.44). Operational descriptions and free-text lines such as 'REFER TO DIVISION 28 ...' are set-level notes, excluded. In 001 the line 'SEALS | BY DOOR / FRAME MANUFACTURER' under RAIN DRIP starts its own row (row spacing, not wrap spacing) and has no qty/unit, so it is its own component. Wrapped catalog lines are joined with one space even after a trailing hyphen (e.g. 'LXRX-LC-QEL-9849-EO-CON- SNB 24 VDC', 'RX-QEL-9847-L-DT-F-LBR- 06SS-CON 24 VDC'); only the finish '630-'/'316' is joined without a space. Set 030's hardware list ends on p.40 but its operational description continues on p.41, so pages=[40,41]. The catalog/cut-sheet and electrified icons between columns are ignored.",
